{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: The multimodal configs (038/039) show a large jump from the best RNA-only result (0.653) to ~0.725, but we have only one image-only data point (ResNet50, single-profile, 0.208), which tells us almost nothing about how well the ViT-L encoder captures useful signal. We cannot yet decompose whether the multimodal gain comes from genuinely complementary image information or merely from a larger model. 2) What this tests: config_015 (image-only, multiprofile, ViT-L, transformer) isolates the image modality with the same strong encoder used in the top multimodal configs, directly measuring how much predictive signal the image carries independently. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, this single-variable test reduces the largest remaining uncertainty—whether the image branch is contributing real information or is a dead weight. If ViT-L image-only is strong (>0.5), the multimodal gain is partly additive image information and we should invest in image-side improvements; if it remains weak, the multimodal gain likely comes from cross-modal interaction, guiding us toward fusion/aggregation refinements. This knowledge is prerequisite for making informed exploitation decisions in subsequent experiments, making it more informative than marginal tweaks (e.g., concat vs weighted) that show only ~0.4% differences."
}

